  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: netty-handler 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released io.netty:netty-handler 4.1.100.Final-rhlw-00001 with backported fixes for CVE-2025-24970, CVE-2026-44249, CVE-2026-45416, CVE-2026-50010, CVE-2026-75595, and CVE-2026-75596.\n\nCVE-2025-24970: SslHandler doesn't correctly validate packets which can lead to native crash when using native SSLEngine\n\nCVE-2026-44249: Netty has an IPv6 Subnet Filter Bypass via Incorrect Comparator Masking\n\nCVE-2026-45416: Netty: SNI handler pre-allocates up to 16 MiB from nine attacker bytes\n\nCVE-2026-50010: Netty's wrapping plain trust manager silently disables hostname verification\n\nCVE-2026-75595: Netty: SNI Routing Bypass via Fragmented TLS ClientHello Causing Fallback to Default SslContext\n\nCVE-2026-75596: Netty: Fragmented ClientHello records trigger quadratic pre-handshake reassembly in default SNI parsing\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for io.netty:netty-handler 4.1.100.Final from Maven Central.",
